  "caption": "Quinn joined a basketball team (height is a state of mind), landed on a teammate's foot and rolled an ankle. Two weeks later it felt fine, so Quinn played on and rolled it again.\n\nFeeling fine isn't the same as fully rehabbed: strength and balance often lag behind the pain, and all that jumping loads the knees too.\n\nWhat often helps: balance, landing and agility training, taping or bracing after a sprain, building calf and thigh strength, and keeping an eye on total load, especially for teens on several teams.\n\nNot being able to weight-bear, a lot of swelling, repeated rolling, or a jammed finger that stays swollen are worth getting checked.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
